[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/app/output/final_report.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Global Intentional Homicide Trends: A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023)</title>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.4/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: #1a3a5c;
    --accent: #c0392b;
    --accent2: #2980b9;
    --accent3: #27ae60;
    --bg: #f8f9fa;
    --card-bg: #ffffff;
    --text: #2c3e50;
    --text-light: #5d6d7e;
    --border: #e0e4e8;
    --shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Roboto, Oxygen, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary) 0%, #2c5f8a 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 48px 0 36px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .header h1 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
  .header .subtitle { font-size: 1.05rem; opacity: 0.85; font-weight: 300; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

  /* KPI Dashboard */
  .kpi-strip {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin: -28px auto 32px;
    max-width: 1100px;
    padding: 0 24px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .kpi-card {
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px 16px;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .kpi-card:nth-child(2) { border-top-color: var(--accent2); }
  .kpi-card:nth-child(3) { border-top-color: #e67e22; }
  .kpi-card:nth-child(4) { border-top-color: var(--accent3); }
  .kpi-card:nth-child(5) { border-top-color: #8e44ad; }
  .kpi-value { font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); line-height: 1.2; }
  .kpi-label { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-light); margin-top: 6px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; font-weight: 600; }

  .section {
    background: var(--card-bg);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .section h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin: 20px 0 10px;
  }
  .section p, .section li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .section ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .chart-wrap {
    position: relative;
    margin: 20px 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .chart-wrap.half { width: 48%; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; }
  .chart-row { display: flex; gap: 4%; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* Data tables */
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.88rem; margin: 14px 0; }
  th { background: var(--primary); color: white; padding: 10px 12px; text-align: left; font-weight: 600; }
  td { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #f4f6f7; }
  .tag-decrease { background: #d4efdf; color: #1e8449; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .tag-increase { background: #fadbd8; color: #c0392b; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.82rem; }

  .callout {
    background: #eaf2f8;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent2);
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 16px 0;
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .callout.warning {
    background: #fef9e7;
    border-left-color: #e67e22;
  }
  .callout strong { color: var(--primary); }

  .footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 28px;
    color: var(--text-light);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .chart-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .chart-wrap.half { width: 100%; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .header h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Global Intentional Homicide Trends</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023) &mdash; Based on UNODC Crime Trends Survey Data</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- KPI Dashboard -->
<div class="kpi-strip">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">2.48</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Global Median Rate (2021)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">3.2x</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Male-to-Female Ratio</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">51.9</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Highest National Rate (Jamaica)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">&minus;40.7%</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Median Rate Decline (1990s &rarr; 2020s)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">58.2%</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Reporting Coverage (2021)</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- Section 1: Global Overview -->
<div class="section" id="global-overview">
  <h2>1. Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
  <p>The global median intentional homicide rate has declined markedly over the past three decades, falling from 3.35 per 100,000 in 1990 to 1.84 in 2023. However, this headline improvement masks substantial variation: the mean rate remains elevated (7.68 in 2021) due to a long right tail of high-violence countries, and the interquartile range remains wide. The number of reporting countries peaked at 162 in 2008 before declining, particularly in the 2020s, which complicates interpretation of recent trends.</p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartGlobalTrend" height="110"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key finding:</strong> The global median homicide rate fell by approximately 41% from the 1990s (3.96) to the 2020s (2.35), while the mean rate declined only 7% (8.27 to 7.71). This divergence indicates that extreme outliers continue to skew the distribution, and improvement has been uneven.
  </div>

  <h3>Decade-over-Decade Trajectory</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Decade</th><th>Mean Rate</th><th>Median Rate</th><th>Change in Median</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1990s</td><td>8.27</td><td>3.96</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2000s</td><td>8.51</td><td>3.33</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;15.9%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>2010s</td><td>7.70</td><td>2.62</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;21.3%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>2020s</td><td>7.71</td><td>2.35</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;10.3%</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Reporting Coverage Over Time</h3>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartCoverage" height="80"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p class="callout warning">Coverage peaked at 162 countries in 2008 and declined to just 84 countries in 2023 (41.8% of the 201 countries in the dataset). The decline in recent years means that 2020s figures should be interpreted with caution &mdash; they may reflect selection bias as much as genuine trend changes.</p>
</div>

<!-- Section 2: Regional Comparison -->
<div class="section" id="regional-comparison">
  <h2>2. Regional &amp; Country-Level Comparison</h2>
  <p>Homicide rates vary enormously by region. Countries in the Americas &mdash; particularly Central America and the Caribbean &mdash; consistently record the highest rates globally, while Europe and Asia report the lowest. South America's median rate has declined substantially from the 1990s but remains well above the global average.</p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartRegional" height="120"></canvas>
  </div>

  <h3>Top 10 Countries by Homicide Rate (2021)</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Country</th><th>Rate per 100,000</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>Jamaica</td><td>51.94</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>South Africa</td><td>40.94</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>Saint Lucia</td><td>39.21</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>Honduras</td><td>38.20</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td>Belize</td><td>31.62</td></tr>
      <tr><td>6</td><td>Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</td><td>31.12</td></tr>
      <tr><td>7</td><td>Turks and Caicos Islands</td><td>30.94</td></tr>
      <tr><td>8</td><td>Trinidad and Tobago</td><td>30.11</td></tr>
      <tr><td>9</td><td>Bahamas</td><td>30.02</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10</td><td>Saint Kitts and Nevis</td><td>29.94</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="callout">7 of the 10 highest-rate countries in 2021 are Caribbean or Central American nations, underscoring the concentration of extreme homicide levels in that subregion.</div>

  <h3>Bottom 10 Countries by Homicide Rate (2021)</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Country</th><th>Rate per 100,000</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>201</td><td>Holy See</td><td>0.00</td></tr>
      <tr><td>200</td><td>Bahrain</td><td>0.07</td></tr>
      <tr><td>199</td><td>Singapore</td><td>0.11</td></tr>
      <tr><td>198</td><td>Japan</td><td>0.23</td></tr>
      <tr><td>197</td><td>Oman</td><td>0.24</td></tr>
      <tr><td>196</td><td>Hong Kong</td><td>0.31</td></tr>
      <tr><td>195</td><td>Qatar</td><td>0.32</td></tr>
      <tr><td>194</td><td>Malta</td><td>0.38</td></tr>
      <tr><td>193</td><td>Slovenia</td><td>0.43</td></tr>
      <tr><td>192</td><td>Macao</td><td>0.43</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartTopBottom" height="100"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 3: Gender Disparity -->
<div class="section" id="sex-disparity">
  <h2>3. Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>
  <p>Males are consistently far more likely to be homicide victims than females. The global median male-to-female homicide rate ratio stands at approximately 3.2:1, meaning the typical country's male homicide rate is over three times its female rate. This ratio has remained relatively stable across the observation period, fluctuating between 2.7 and 3.8.</p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartSexRatio" height="100"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-wrap half">
      <canvas id="chartMaleFemaleTrend" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap half">
      <canvas id="chartSexByAge" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key finding:</strong> The male-to-female ratio peaked at 3.8:1 around 2010 and has since moderated to roughly 3.2:1. While this narrowing is encouraging, it reflects both a decline in male victimization and persistently high female victimization in certain regions &mdash; not solely progress. The gender gap is most extreme in the 15&ndash;29 and 30&ndash;44 age groups, where male rates are approximately 3&ndash;4 times female rates.
  </div>

  <h3>Gender Disparity by Age Group (Median Rates)</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Age Group</th><th>Male Rate</th><th>Female Rate</th><th>M:F Ratio</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>0&ndash;14 (Children)</td><td>0.33</td><td>0.26</td><td>1.3:1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>15&ndash;29 (Youth)</td><td>2.74</td><td>0.86</td><td>3.2:1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>30&ndash;44 (Young Adults)</td><td>4.08</td><td>1.39</td><td>2.9:1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>45&ndash;59 (Middle-aged)</td><td>3.43</td><td>1.06</td><td>3.2:1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>60+ (Elderly)</td><td>2.12</td><td>0.95</td><td>2.2:1</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The gender gap is smallest among children (1.3:1) and the elderly (2.2:1), and widest among working-age males. This pattern aligns with research linking male homicide victimization to involvement in gang activity, organized crime, and interpersonal violence in the 15&ndash;44 age range.</p>
</div>

<!-- Section 4: Age Group Analysis -->
<div class="section" id="age-group-analysis">
  <h2>4. Age Group Analysis</h2>
  <p>Homicide risk is strongly stratified by age. Young and middle-aged adults (30&ndash;44) face the highest median homicide rate (2.26 per 100,000), followed by the 15&ndash;29 youth cohort (1.46). Children under 15 are the least affected group, with a median rate of just 0.31. All age groups have seen declining rates from the 2000s to the 2020s.</p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chartAgeGroup" height="100"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Youth vulnerability:</strong> While the 15&ndash;29 age group does not have the highest median rate overall, it has the widest spread &mdash; in high-violence countries, youth homicide rates can exceed 50 per 100,000. The 30&ndash;44 group shows the most consistent elevation across countries, suggesting that working-age adults face structural risk factors beyond youth-specific dynamics.
  </div>

  <h3>Age-Specific Trends by Decade</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Age Group</th><th>2000s Median</th><th>2010s Median</th><th>2020s Median</th><th>Change (2000s&rarr;2020s)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>0&ndash;14</td><td>N/A</td><td>0.32</td><td>0.23</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;28%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>15&ndash;29</td><td>N/A</td><td>1.61</td><td>1.26</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;22%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>30&ndash;44</td><td>2.62</td><td>2.24</td><td>2.02</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;23%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>45&ndash;59</td><td>N/A</td><td>N/A</td><td>N/A</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
      <tr><td>60+</td><td>1.50</td><td>1.29</td><td>1.20</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;20%</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="callout warning">Age-disaggregated data coverage is more limited than overall data, with substantial gaps in the 1990s. Cross-decade comparisons for some age groups are not feasible due to insufficient observations.</p>
</div>

<!-- Section 5: Notable Trends & Outliers -->
<div class="section" id="notable-trends">
  <h2>5. Notable Country-Level Trends &amp; Outliers</h2>
  <p>While the global trend is downward, individual country trajectories diverge sharply. The analysis below compares average rates in the early observation period (1990&ndash;1995) with the late period (2018&ndash;2023) for countries with early-period rates above 1.0 per 100,000.</p>

  <h3>Largest Declines (Early 1990s &rarr; Late 2010s/2020s)</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Early Rate (1990&ndash;95)</th><th>Late Rate (2018&ndash;23)</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Montserrat</td><td>5.22</td><td>0.00</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;100.0%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Singapore</td><td>1.54</td><td>0.14</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;90.8%</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tajikistan</td><td>9.58</td><td>0.89</td><td><span class="tag-decrease">&minus;90.7%</span></td></tr>
